  "limitations": [
    "This is a participating-storage budget, not a bound on total native memory or RSS. Arrow ownership graphs and other ordinary Rust/native allocations remain outside enforcement.",
    "Infallible constructors or cloning on allocator-backed storage retain allocation-error-handler behavior. Strict lifecycle tests exercise converted fallible paths; they are not a proof that every public infallible Kernel API is recoverable.",
    "DHAT stack groups attribute live requested allocations, not exact enforced charge at that same instant. Pending growth, canonical allocations before profiler start, and internal realloc copies affect comparison. No exact budget-counter callback at the global heap peak was captured.",
    "Unprofiled Rust/RSS totals include the local reference engine and harness. Independent peak ratios do not measure coverage; profiler behavior/timing can differ from unprofiled runs.",
    "Terminal metadata-plan execution and declarative commit are outside this lifecycle.",
    "One repetition per correctness case does not establish latency percentiles or performance regressions."
  ]
